250
00:29:27,808 --> 00:29:30,101
if she wants to take control
of murthehelp.

251
00:29:30,102 --> 00:29:33,021
She'll be a bit distracted
when she captures my uncle.

252
00:29:33,689 --> 00:29:36,942
In the meantime, we'll gather intel
from the Code Purples and the mole.

253
00:29:38,110 --> 00:29:40,236
I'm Jeong Jian, thanks for coming.

254
00:29:40,237 --> 00:29:42,781
We need to pull in as many Code Reds
as possible.

255
00:29:46,326 --> 00:29:48,495
Once Kusanagi knows our location…

256
00:29:51,331 --> 00:29:53,250
they'll come to eliminate us.

257
00:30:05,971 --> 00:30:07,681
It's a trap!

258
00:30:12,853 --> 00:30:16,440
What happened? Report.
What's going on, damn it?

259
00:30:17,691 --> 00:30:19,525
If the operation succeeds,

260
00:30:19,526 --> 00:30:22,529
Babylon's regular forces
will be completely isolated.

261
00:30:23,280 --> 00:30:24,281
Wait a minute.

262
00:30:25,866 --> 00:30:27,909
Once Babylon extracts the data…

263
00:30:29,536 --> 00:30:31,121
they might kill Jinman.

264
00:30:34,458 --> 00:30:35,459
Yep.

265
00:30:37,210 --> 00:30:38,587
We'll have to trust her then.

266
00:30:40,881 --> 00:30:42,299
The woman who brought him in.

267
00:30:44,217 --> 00:30:45,343
I'm heading out now.

268
00:30:46,970 --> 00:30:48,680
I have your niece to capture.

269
00:30:50,432 --> 00:30:52,642
Do you really think you can win?

270
00:30:56,855 --> 00:30:58,774
This isn't a fight I'm trying to win.

271
00:31:01,276 --> 00:31:03,652
I was trying to protect my niece.

272
00:31:03,653 --> 00:31:06,782
After all, it's my fault
that her life ended up the way it is now.

273
00:31:08,784 --> 00:31:11,119
But we sacrificed too much for it.

274
00:31:18,251 --> 00:31:19,377
I'm sorry about…

275
00:31:20,670 --> 00:31:21,671
your brother.

276
00:31:29,137 --> 00:31:30,347
The thing is…

277
00:31:32,557 --> 00:31:35,227
I always knew that someday
this moment would come.

278
00:31:39,731 --> 00:31:43,610
My younger brother and I
were raised by yakuza.

279
00:31:44,694 --> 00:31:46,363
I think I was around 10…

280
00:31:48,990 --> 00:31:52,994
when our clan boss took his revenge
on our father.

281
00:31:54,287 --> 00:31:56,331
He made us stay there and watch him do it.

282
00:31:57,624 --> 00:32:02,212
He told us later that when he slit
our father's throat, we didn't blink.

283
00:32:03,088 --> 00:32:05,966
He said that we had
this look in our eyes then.

284
00:32:07,384 --> 00:32:10,137
That we didn't flinch or turn away.

285
00:32:13,265 --> 00:32:16,101
That's when he decided
to raise us as yakuzas.

286
00:32:16,893 --> 00:32:18,645
That look in our eyes.

287
00:32:22,190 --> 00:32:24,901
When I saw your niece,
I saw the same look in hers.

288
00:32:25,652 --> 00:32:26,820
You have it too.

289
00:32:28,530 --> 00:32:29,990
And I know I still have it.

290
00:32:31,116 --> 00:32:32,909
That's just the type of people we are.

291
00:32:33,702 --> 00:32:37,788
If you keep a lion locked in a cage,
her claws will get dull.

292
00:32:37,789 --> 00:32:39,583
She'll forget her own nature.

293
00:32:44,504 --> 00:32:46,464
I guess the choice is yours now.

294
00:32:47,215 --> 00:32:50,385
Not true. It's Jian's to make.

295
00:32:51,553 --> 00:32:53,471
Considering the bad choices I made,

296
00:32:54,556 --> 00:32:56,849
I don't think it's a luxury I deserve.

297
00:32:56,850 --> 00:32:59,393
Jian has already made her choice,

298
00:32:59,394 --> 00:33:02,564
so what I'll do now is protect her
with everything in me.

299
00:33:10,322 --> 00:33:11,656
I think this is…

300
00:33:14,201 --> 00:33:15,577
as far as I can go.

301
00:33:24,044 --> 00:33:27,547
Do you think… we can meet again one day?

302
00:33:30,550 --> 00:33:31,843
If we're still breathing.

303
00:33:33,428 --> 00:33:36,014
Looks like that drink
will have to wait again.

304
00:33:40,227 --> 00:33:41,436
My name is…

305
00:33:43,480 --> 00:33:44,564
Ichika, okay?

306
00:33:47,108 --> 00:33:49,778
Takimoto Ichika.

307
00:34:09,464 --> 00:34:10,798
Report this to Q right away.

308
00:34:10,799 --> 00:34:11,800
Shit, we're fucked.

309
00:34:15,887 --> 00:34:19,181
Q, come in. Answer me now!

310
00:34:28,024 --> 00:34:30,901
- What? I'm busy here.
-  We have a serious problem.

311
00:34:30,902 --> 00:34:32,152
The higher-ups know everything.

312
00:34:32,153 --> 00:34:34,446
You need to come
to the office immediately.

313
00:34:34,447 --> 00:34:37,117
I was told "a certain person"
is waiting for you on a video call.

314
00:34:41,913 --> 00:34:42,914
Shit.

315
00:34:44,416 --> 00:34:46,126
Has headquarters said anything?

316
00:34:50,714 --> 00:34:52,716
Shit. No.

317
00:35:17,324 --> 00:35:19,534
Oh, shit. Son of a bitch.

318
00:35:20,952 --> 00:35:21,953
Don't move!

319
00:35:24,748 --> 00:35:25,749
It's all right.

320
00:35:31,379 --> 00:35:35,008
Hey, lower the guns.
Yeah, it's all right. It's dangerous.

321
00:35:54,819 --> 00:35:55,986
-  Yes?
-  K,

322
00:35:55,987 --> 00:35:57,447
pull out of there immediately

323
00:35:57,739 --> 00:35:59,574
- and return to headquarters.
-  Sorry?

324
00:36:00,784 --> 00:36:01,868
Do you mean right now?

325
00:36:03,411 --> 00:36:05,287
We're in the middle of an operation.

326
00:36:05,288 --> 00:36:08,666
From now on, that
operation has nothing to do with Babylon.

327
00:36:08,667 --> 00:36:10,543
Return to base. Immediately.

328
00:36:15,256 --> 00:36:16,466
Huh?

329
00:36:17,634 --> 00:36:20,053
It's not like I'm busy as hell
or anything.

330
00:36:21,054 --> 00:36:22,764
If it's urgent, he should come himself.

331
00:36:57,090 --> 00:36:58,091
Where to?

332
00:37:06,391 --> 00:37:07,892
Let's go home.

333
00:37:57,233 --> 00:37:58,984
Hey, did you see
the bus footage?

334
00:37:58,985 --> 00:38:00,612
Yeah, what a crazy bitch.

335
00:38:06,993 --> 00:38:09,204
I knew something was off
from the start. Shit.

336
00:38:53,039 --> 00:38:56,835
Are… you fucking kidding me?

337
00:39:34,080 --> 00:39:35,123
DISABLE SECURITY PROTOCOL?

338
00:39:50,221 --> 00:39:51,389
Stay out here.

339
00:40:33,681 --> 00:40:36,601
You sneaky motherfucker.

340
00:40:58,039 --> 00:41:01,625
Hey, main gate.
Stop that vehicle from entering!

341
00:41:01,626 --> 00:41:02,918
Stop that goddamn bus!

342
00:41:02,919 --> 00:41:04,294
That the reason the bus exploded

343
00:41:04,295 --> 00:41:05,712
- that night was…
-  Can't you hear me?

344
00:41:05,713 --> 00:41:07,757
- …to cover up Bale killing Jun.
-  Do you wanna die too?

345
00:41:17,433 --> 00:41:18,434
Okay.

346
00:41:21,729 --> 00:41:24,816
Seems like Operation Empty House
is a success.

347
00:41:25,942 --> 00:41:29,862
All we're doing is using her own playbook
and turning it back on her.

348
00:41:57,932 --> 00:42:00,685
How the hell did that bastard
get out of that damn cell?

349
00:42:27,670 --> 00:42:28,671
What should we do?

350
00:42:53,821 --> 00:42:56,908
Let's just wait. Just a bit.

351
00:43:06,584 --> 00:43:09,003
Lower your guns.
Everyone, guns down.

352
00:43:11,672 --> 00:43:12,673
Open the gate.

353
00:43:18,262 --> 00:43:20,180
You all heard, I'm sure,

354
00:43:20,181 --> 00:43:23,684
most of Babylon's fighters have been
buried under tons of rubble in our mine.

355
00:43:24,435 --> 00:43:27,229
We expect that some number
of forces will remain,

356
00:43:27,230 --> 00:43:29,190
but our target is only…

357
00:43:30,441 --> 00:43:31,776
Kusanagi Jin.

358
00:43:32,693 --> 00:43:34,444
If they aren't targets,

359
00:43:34,445 --> 00:43:38,324
please refrain from engaging with any
unarmed personnel that are still inside.

360
00:43:39,784 --> 00:43:41,202
Just priority one.

361
00:43:46,082 --> 00:43:50,043
So these trashy little vermin
really want to come after me, huh?

362
00:43:50,044 --> 00:43:53,840
These fucking rat bastards.
I have to do everything around here.

363
00:43:57,802 --> 00:44:01,264
In the end, you're all you got.
Fucking alone.

364
00:44:10,314 --> 00:44:11,315
Shit.

365
00:44:36,382 --> 00:44:37,383
Three o'clock.

366
00:45:14,503 --> 00:45:16,547
You dressed correctly for the occasion.

367
00:45:34,649 --> 00:45:35,650
Let's do this.

368
00:45:36,525 --> 00:45:38,277
The real negotiation begins now.

369
00:45:42,198 --> 00:45:43,199
Hey!

370
00:45:46,202 --> 00:45:48,996
Come and get me, you ragtag motherfuckers!

371
00:46:00,007 --> 00:46:01,466
Uncle…

372
00:46:01,467 --> 00:46:02,593
Are you okay?

373
00:46:09,058 --> 00:46:11,894
Hey! Kusanagi's in front
of the situation room!

374
00:46:34,166 --> 00:46:35,334
Jian, get up!

375
00:46:43,843 --> 00:46:44,927
Hold as long as you can.

376
00:47:01,235 --> 00:47:02,653
Not a fucking chance.

377
00:47:18,336 --> 00:47:19,337
We're connected.

378
00:47:35,436 --> 00:47:38,272
So you are Jeong Jinman.

379
00:47:45,321 --> 00:47:48,824
It's been 12 years since I've had
to smell this disgusting gunpowder!

380
00:48:01,045 --> 00:48:05,257
Are you trying to blackmail us
with something Kusanagi did on her own?

381
00:48:07,051 --> 00:48:08,552
That seems a little weak.

382
00:48:09,095 --> 00:48:11,806
I'm just relaying to you
what your employee did…

383
00:48:12,723 --> 00:48:14,892
during her time here
leading Babylon Korea.

384
00:48:15,976 --> 00:48:19,105
The blackmail would be the data
we have on the server.

385
00:48:30,449 --> 00:48:32,243
What is it that you want?

386
00:48:32,868 --> 00:48:35,663
Peaceful coexistence
between murthehelp and Babylon.

387
00:48:36,497 --> 00:48:37,706
That's all I want.

388
00:48:44,046 --> 00:48:45,714
"Peaceful coexistence."

389
00:48:48,217 --> 00:48:51,262
Do you think
such an idealistic relationship can last?

390
00:48:52,596 --> 00:48:57,059
Peace isn't exactly… good
for our line of business.

391
00:48:59,770 --> 00:49:03,064
I'm sure you know this
since you were once a part of Babylon,

392
00:49:03,065 --> 00:49:05,859
but we will not hesitate
to break any lasting peace

393
00:49:05,860 --> 00:49:07,653
for the sake of business.

394
00:49:08,362 --> 00:49:13,409
Humans have been killing each other
for thousands of years now,

395
00:49:14,452 --> 00:49:18,831
and in the end your murthehelp is banking
on that same human nature,

396
00:49:19,498 --> 00:49:21,500
making profit off human lives.

397
00:49:22,626 --> 00:49:25,880
For someone like that
to be talking about peace…

398
00:49:28,591 --> 00:49:29,967
what a contradiction.

399
00:49:34,054 --> 00:49:37,391
There have been times of peace,
no matter how brief they were.

400
00:49:38,434 --> 00:49:39,560
In that case…

401
00:49:41,520 --> 00:49:43,355
we can call it a ceasefire.

402
00:49:48,277 --> 00:49:51,489
If Babylon were to accept my proposal,

403
00:49:52,448 --> 00:49:54,909
I won't need murthehelp. Not anymore.

404
00:50:07,963 --> 00:50:10,591
-  Uncle Cheolseung!
- Don't worry, I'm okay.

405
00:50:16,680 --> 00:50:19,683
Who the hell said
you could negotiate by yourselves?

406
00:50:22,520 --> 00:50:23,812
Put the gun down.

407
00:50:24,939 --> 00:50:26,649
Your work here is finished now.

408
00:50:29,109 --> 00:50:33,696
My methods were never a problem before.
You'd just turn a blind eye, didn't you?

409
00:50:33,697 --> 00:50:37,535
I did it all for the sake of Babylon.
And now what? You're firing me?

410
00:50:38,577 --> 00:50:41,496
All because of a lapse of judgment?

411
00:50:41,497 --> 00:50:45,417
It was never
"all for the sake of Babylon" to you.

412
00:50:46,168 --> 00:50:48,170
You were only ever loyal to yourself.

413
00:50:52,049 --> 00:50:53,133
Fuck that!

414
00:50:55,678 --> 00:50:57,345
You pathetic little shits.

415
00:51:37,136 --> 00:51:38,137
Mr. Jeong Jinman…

416
00:51:40,556 --> 00:51:45,019
you and I are both people
who walk alongside the specter of death.

417
00:51:47,187 --> 00:51:50,482
I swear, as long as I remain here…

418
00:51:52,943 --> 00:51:54,653
I'll honor our ceasefire.

419
00:51:55,446 --> 00:51:56,614
We have a truce.

420
00:51:58,616 --> 00:52:01,952
Then I'll…
take care of business over here.

421
00:52:03,245 --> 00:52:04,246
But first…

422
00:52:05,998 --> 00:52:07,707
I'll make this clear.

423
00:52:07,708 --> 00:52:10,835
Even if the most trivial piece of data
leaks out,

424
00:52:10,836 --> 00:52:13,964
for example, let's say,
what a client had for dinner

425
00:52:14,673 --> 00:52:16,883
or the name of our client's dog.

426
00:52:16,884 --> 00:52:18,886
If anything were to leak out,

427
00:52:19,637 --> 00:52:21,013
then you and your niece,

428
00:52:21,764 --> 00:52:25,684
along with anyone
ever involved with your operation,

429
00:52:27,353 --> 00:52:28,479
will all disappear.

430
00:52:32,983 --> 00:52:35,027
Make sure you honor your end.

431
00:52:40,908 --> 00:52:43,869
We'll talk again, Jeong Jinman.

432
00:52:45,162 --> 00:52:46,205
And you too…

433
00:52:48,290 --> 00:52:49,416
Jeong Jian.

434
00:53:36,380 --> 00:53:37,840
Did everyone make it out?

435
00:54:29,224 --> 00:54:30,350
Now what's the plan?

436
00:54:33,103 --> 00:54:34,396
You're asking me that?

437
00:54:48,702 --> 00:54:49,703
Then now…

438
00:54:54,249 --> 00:54:56,834
…listen up, Jeong Jinman.

439
00:54:56,835 --> 00:55:01,632
A SHOP FOR KILLERS 2

440
00:55:09,681 --> 00:55:11,141
BASED ON THE NOVEL BY KANG JI YOUNG
